# clinical v1.20 — WARNING. Two clinical:narrativeText values on one document.
#
# WHY THIS EXACT RECORD, AND WHY IT IS THE CHANGE MOST WORTH PINNING. This is
# not an invented edge case; it is the scenario clinical:NarrativeTextCountShape's
# own comment in clinical.shapes.ttl names as why the constraint had to be
# relaxed. A C-CDA document carrying two sections that share one LOINC section
# code converts onto ONE section record, because that record is keyed on the
# document, the section code and the source, and the identity scheme does not
# yet distinguish the two sections. Both narratives land on
# clinical:narrativeText, correctly, under the identity Cascade has today. Here
# the shared code is 51847-2 (Assessment and Plan): an addendum note filed a
# second "Assessment and Plan" section rather than replacing the first, and the
# converter has no way to tell the two apart.
#
# THROUGH v1.19 THIS WAS sh:Violation, ON clinical:ClinicalDocumentShape
# ITSELF. It never fired, because the narrative was written under an
# undeclared spelling (cascade:narrativeText / clinical:content) that no shape
# reached. clinical:narrativeText being written for the first time, per the
# rest of this release, is what makes the constraint reachable at all -- and
# rejecting this record outright would have meant re-keying the section
# record and re-minting every existing narrative node, so v1.20 reports the
# count instead of rejecting it. sh:Warning is the shape's answer, not a
# general policy: it applies to this one constraint, on this one property,
# because of what re-keying would cost, not because every constraint this
# release touches was softened.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXTURE ASSERTS, AND WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT. It asserts
# that clinical:NarrativeTextCountShape's own sh:maxCount 1 fires as a single
# sh:Warning naming clinical:narrativeText. It asserts equally that NOTHING
# REJECTS the record. clinical:documentType and the two legacy narrative
# spellings are left out entirely, so this fixture is evidence about the
# count constraint alone and not about DocumentTypeShape or
# NarrativeTextSpellingShape.
#
# RED, NOT SILENT, AGAINST THE PREVIOUS PIN. Against clinical v1.19, this same
# record is REJECTED: clinical:ClinicalDocumentShape's own sh:maxCount 1 on
# clinical:narrativeText fires at its default severity, sh:Violation. A
# .WARN.ttl fixture asserted here before v1.20 would have failed with
# VIOLATIONS, not passed -- the polarity this fixture claims is new with this
# release, not merely newly exercised.
#
# Fully synthetic: invented clinic, clinician, visit and section content.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:d0c00116-0000-4000-8000-000000000007> a clinical:ClinicalDocument ;
    clinical:displayName "Progress Note" ;
    clinical:documentDate "2031-04-02"^^xsd:date ;
    clinical:status "final" ;
    clinical:documentReferenceStatus "current" ;

    # Two "Assessment and Plan" sections (LOINC 51847-2), converted onto one
    # section record because the record's identity does not yet separate them.
    clinical:narrativeText "Assessment and Plan: Hypertension, well controlled on lisinopril 20 mg daily. Continue current regimen and recheck blood pressure in six weeks." ;
    clinical:narrativeText "Assessment and Plan (addendum): Patient called after the visit reporting occasional lightheadedness on standing. Advised to rise slowly and to report recurrence; no medication change made pending recheck." ;

    clinical:documentAuthorName "Dara Fennimore, MD" ;
    clinical:fhirResourceId "DocumentReference/dr-56413" ;
    clinical:fhirResourceType "DocumentReference" ;
    clinical:importedAt "2031-04-05T09:40:12-05:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    clinical:sourceEHR "Meridian Health System" ;
    cascade:sourceIdentity "org:meridian" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.4" .
